@prefix tmk:     <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/> .
@prefix tmkc:    <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/time>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "TM-Knowledge — time module"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment """Dates, currency and what this corpus cannot answer about time.

The honest headline: **point-in-time questions are out of the pilot scope draft
and the snapshot cannot support them.** There is no corpus-level version stamp
(Q-05); the amendment history is the upstream repository's git history, and
answering 'what guidance was current on «date»' properly needs a full-history
clone, which is a different data strategy rather than a different query. CQ-0014
is marked out of scope on the strength of that line.

What the module does carry is the currency mechanism that actually works:
staleness by content hash. An assertion whose source hash no longer matches the
pin is stale and returns to review. That is Stage 10's whole incremental
mechanism and it needs no version stamp."""@en-AU ;
    owl:imports <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/provenance> ;
    owl:versionInfo "draft — not approved" .

tmk:AuthorityStatus a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Authority status"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether an authority is current, superseded or repealed."@en-AU .

tmk:Current a tmk:AuthorityStatus ; rdfs:label "current"@en-AU .

tmk:Superseded a tmk:AuthorityStatus ; rdfs:label "superseded"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "'Every superseded instruction has a status date' — one of the six starting SHACL rules."@en-AU .

tmk:NotHeld a tmk:AuthorityStatus ; rdfs:label "not held"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment """Cited by the corpus and held nowhere in the programme.

Not a defect and not a gap to be filled by guessing: s 114 of the *Trade Marks
Act 1905* is cited by Part 29.3.1, the instrument is not in this corpus, and it
can be neither excluded (the Manual relies on it) nor resolved (Q-24). 17
distinct refs cited from the in-scope chunks are in this state, and CQ-0020 asks
for exactly this list."""@en-AU .

tmk:authorityStatus a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:range tmk:AuthorityStatus ;
    rdfs:label "authority status"@en-AU .

tmk:statusDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:label "status date"@en-AU .

tmk:capturedAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "captured at"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "When upstream captured the passage. The nearest thing this corpus has to a currency date, and it is a capture time, not an in-force date."@en-AU .

tmk:lastAmended a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tmk:Page ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "last amended"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual page's own amendment note where it carries one. Page-level and self-reported — not a version stamp, and not comparable across pages."@en-AU .

tmk:isStale a owl:DatatypeProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tmk:Assertion ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "is stale"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The assertion's `tmk:sourceContentHash` no longer matches the pinned snapshot: the passage under it moved. Computed at build time, never asserted by hand."@en-AU .
